Keeps `public/` in git, because the Dockerfile copies it.

The five files that used to be here — file.svg, globe.svg, next.svg,
vercel.svg, window.svg — were create-next-app scaffold and were referenced by
nothing. The favicon is not among them: it lives at `src/app/favicon.ico`,
which is where the App Router looks for it.

Git does not track empty directories, so deleting the last file here would
delete the directory, and `COPY --from=builder /app/public ./public` in the
Dockerfile would fail the build on the next deploy. Dropping that COPY instead
would be worse: the day somebody adds a genuine static file here it would
silently not ship, which is the kind of thing nobody debugs quickly.
